How the scatter works:
Two layers. Big things (trees + large boulders) sit on a coarse grid so they keep their spacing; small things (bushes, flowers, tufts, small rocks) fill in on a finer grid. That keeps it from looking like a wall of trees.
Plentiful vs. scarce. Each spot's fill chance rides a low-frequency noise field, so you naturally get dense groves and thickets in some areas and open clearings in others — but spread evenly across the whole map, not clumped in one corner.
Seated + static. Everything is randomly rotated, seated so its base rests on the ground (regardless of the model's pivot), and fully anchored so nothing tips or falls. Any stray scripts/cameras inside the assets are stripped out so they stay pure scenery.
House yard stays clear (nothing spawns within ~132 studs of center), and the build is spread across frames so it won't hard-freeze.
It lands roughly ~150 large + ~1,000 small props. Everything is tunable at the top of MapService.luau — SCATTER_SEED reshuffles the whole layout, and the CELL / MID / SPAN knobs control density (raise CELL or lower MID to thin it out if it feels heavy).
