 The animation asset must be owned by the same account/group that owns the published place. This is the #1 reason animations silently fail. Your repo is under the group businessmans1984-group. If the place is published under that group but the six animations were uploaded to your personal account (or vice-versa), Roblox will refuse to load them and the model just stands there. The teddy bear animation works — which proves that one asset is owned correctly, and that my playback code is fundamentally sound. So the character animations are very likely uploaded under a different owner than the teddy's.
 Rig type must match. An R6 animation only plays on an R6 rig; an R15 animation only on R15. If your game's avatar rig type doesn't match how the animations were authored, they won't play.
 The model needs a Humanoid + Animator and must be in the world.
