5. How grass actually works (important technical detail)
Grass is not individual objects placed by hand. Any part tagged GrassSurface grows grass on its local +Y top face. Two attributes control it: GrassType and GrassHeight. The server subdivides the surface into tiles and tracks grass as numbers, not parts, for performance — visual slabs are spawned and shrink as they take damage.
Two rules that shape the feel:
Clippings pay out only on a fully cleared tile. Partial cuts don't pay. This creates completion pressure.
Clippings drop physically on the ground and are vacuumed up by walking near them. The pickup radius is widened by the Clipping Magnet upgrade.
A held tool is required — no tool, no mowing.
