Three golden rules (from TECH_PLAN.md):
The server is the source of truth. All state, all validation.
Every tunable number lives in GameConfig.luau. No magic numbers scattered in systems.
One module per system.
Loader pattern. init.server.luau requires every ModuleScript in Services/, then calls Init(services) then Start() on each — every step wrapped in pcall so one broken module can't kill the whole server. init.client.luau does the same for Controllers/.
Services (16, server): PlayerDataService, GrassService, MapService, ToolService, ShopService, UpgradeService, ClippingsService, AutoMowerService, GardenerService, QuestService, QuestGiverService, CutsceneService, DistrictService, BackpackService, AdminService
Controllers (11, client): UIController, MowController, ToolController, BackpackController, AutoMowerController, QuestController, CutsceneController, AdminController, DashController, EffectsController
Shared (8): GameConfig, Remotes, Assets, StatCalculator, QuestData, CutsceneData, NpcRig, MowerRig
Networking: all remotes are declared in one central list in Remotes.luau and fetched by name.
Persistence: DataStore, autosave every 2 minutes, save on leave and on BindToClose, session locking to prevent duplicate-server corruption, and a non-saving temporary profile as fallback if a load fails (so a DataStore outage degrades gracefully instead of wiping progress). Profile schema is currently v4 (v2 added gold/diamonds/bag, v3 added auto-mowers, v4 added backpacks), with generous forward migration. Grass state does not persist across sessions — known and deliberately parked.
9. Hard-won lessons and gotchas
These came from real bugs in this project. An AI working on this codebase should know them.
Never call DataStoreService:GetDataStore() at module top level. In an unpublished place it throws, the module fails to load, and every dependent system cascades into attempt to index nil errors far from the real cause.
Avoid \u{} escapes inside backtick interpolated strings — one broke Luau compilation of a whole module. Use utf8.char(0x2022) instead.
Strip embedded scripts from toolbox/free models. They throw LoadUnownedAsset capability errors and run unwanted logic. Both NpcRig.luau and MowerRig.luau exist specifically to sanitize imported models.
The HUD ScreenGui uses ZIndexBehavior.Global. New UI elements must set explicit ZIndex or they render behind the modal (which sits at 10 with an opaque background) and appear to "not exist." Convention: modal 10, cards/lists/notices 11, card children 12, bar fills and bar text 13. This bug was misdiagnosed twice as a data problem. If an element drawn by one file is visible while an element drawn by another is not, suspect layering, not data.
Custom/hand-built NPC rigs may not follow Roblox conventions. The Gardener's rig is internally named Farmer, is hand-built R6 at 0.79 scale, with Motor6Ds hanging off HumanoidRootPart instead of the Torso and joints named after body parts. Adding a standard RootJoint "fixed" the falling torso but broke animation. The correct fix was a Weld on the Torso plus using the rig's own bundled animations.
Player animations require R6 to be enabled in Game Settings. Cutscene animations failed silently until this was set. This is a Studio setting, not a code issue.
Verify files actually persisted after writing. This project has seen silent write failures and a wiped working tree between sessions. Read back, check block balance, confirm the file tail is intact.
